# Session budget

- Do the asked task only. No drive-by refactors or extra markdown.
- Prefer links/retrieval over inlining long docs. Do not open `.cursor/reference/*` unless needed.
- Small commits that survive usage limits. Validate before milestone commits (`scripts/validate.ps1`).
- Lead agent stages/commits; custom subagents must not stage/commit unless the user explicitly asks that agent to.
- Push only when the user asked; never force-push.

## Delegation (conserve expensive reasoning)

- Explore / many file searches → built-in Explore (fast).
- Mechanical implement against existing API/UI/tests/docs → `implementer-glue`.
- After a unit → `verifier` (fast) for validate/test summary.
- Replay/binary/private-replay ambiguity → `decoder-auditor` (Opus high).
- Loopback, rendezvous, hub/mutation, harness online-denial, privacy → `security-auditor` (Fable xhigh, readonly).
- Parent stays on Opus/Fable only while deciding hard design; do not burn it on glue loops.

See `.cursor/reference/model-routing.md` when unsure.
